[00:14.40]1. The meditation of my heart,
[00:20.64]The thoughts I ponder through the day—
[00:28.16]May they be pleasing to you, Lord,
[00:34.96]And keep me steadfast in your way.
[00:43.48]When worries weigh upon my mind
[00:50.48]And make me restless in the night,
[00:57.48]Then may I meditate on you
[01:05.08]And things I know to be upright.
[01:19.20]2. Whatever things are chaste and true,
[01:23.20]Whatever virtue there may be,
[01:30.20]Whatever things well-spoken-of—
[01:35.66]May thoughts of these bring peace to me.
[01:43.66]How precious are your thoughts, O God!
[01:52.80]Beyond all counting is their sum.
[02:25.44]So may I ponder your own words,
[02:32.84]Absorbed in them may I become.